  body
    script(src='https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.2.1/jquery.min.js')
    script(src="https://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/3.3.7/js/bootstrap.min.js" integrity="sha384-Tc5IQib027qvyjSMfHjOMaLkfuWVxZxUPnCJA7l2mCWNIpG9mGCD8wGNIcPD7Txa" crossorigin="anonymous")
    .reveal
      // Any section element inside of this container is displayed as a slide
      .slides
        section
          h1 Dave Borncamp
          img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/headshot.jpg', alt='Dave Borncamp')
          p
            | Principal Technical Manager at
            | SciTec, Inc.
        section
          section
            h2 Background
          section
            h3 Education
            ul
              li 2011 - BA Astronomy @ CU Boulder
              li 2013 - AS Computer Programming and Geographic Information Systems @ FRCC
              li 2016 - MS Computer Science @ Towson University
              li 2021 - Post Graduate Certificate in Space Resource @ Colorado School of Mines
              li 2022 - MS Space Resource @ Colorado School of Mines
          section
            h3 Work
            ul
              li
                | 2010 - 2013: Southwest Research Institute
                ul
                  li Research on Pluto & Kuiper Belt Objects
                  li New Horizons mission support
              br
              li
                | 2013 - 2017 Space Telescope Science Institute
                ul
                  li
                    a(href='#/Functional') Functional Work
                  li
                    a(href='#/Science') Science Work
              br
              li
                | 2017 - 2021: Decipher Technology Studios
                ul
                  li Solutions Team Lead
              br
              li
                | 2021 - 2024: Ball Aerospace
                ul
                  li Chief Software Architect
              br
              li
                | 2024 - present: SciTec, Inc
                ul
                  li Test Infrastructure Lead
        section
          section#Ball
            h2 Ball
            ul
              li Chief Software Architect for Non-Conventional Imaging
              li Tech Lead on multiple programs
              ul
                li Chimera
                li Gremlin
                li StarDust
          section
            h2 Software Architect
            ul
              li Contribute to proposals and system architecture for several programs and see developemt through to delivery.
              li Work with customers to gather requirements and translate them into system designs.
              li Work with internal stakeholders to ensure program delivery.
              li Mentor engineers on best practices and design patterns.
          section
            h2 Chimera and Gremlin
            ul
              li Design and implement multiple services to perform image processing on embedded systems and using Kubernetes for offboard processing.
              li Services are designed to be modular and reusable across multiple programs
              li Technologies used include C++, Python, Docker, Kubernetes, and various image processing libraries.
            h2 StarDust
            ul
              li Designed a Kafka based event driven distributed system to perform near real-time image processing.
              li System is designed to be scalable and reliable using Kubernetes and written in Python.
        section
          section#Decipher
            h2 Decipher
            ul
              li Solutions Team Lead
              ul
                li Core Services
                li ETL Pipeline
                li NLP
          section
            h2 Core Services
            ul
              li Lead a team of developers to build and maintain several core services used by DI2E and DiceLab applications.
              li Services include authentication, authorization, user management, and data storage within the MEME ecosystem.
              li Ensure deployment using GreyMatter sidecars for scalability, reliability, and zero trust security.
          section
            h2 NiFi ETL Pipeline
            ul
              li Built and maintained several NiFi data flows to move and process data using GreyMatter Data.
              li Created a custom NiFi processor to handle complex data transformations called 
              a(href='https://github.com/greymatter-io/nifi-sdk') Greymatter NiFi SDK.
          section
            h2 Multiple Natural Language Processing Services
            ul
              li Develop several microservices to handle Natural Language Processing tasks such as Named Entity Recognition, Part of Speech tagging, and Text Summarization, and coreferencing.
              li Used state of the art NLP libraries such as SpaCy by HuggingFace Transformers to build these services.
              li Also develop a Scala processer using Rozaka to perform NLP tasks in a distributed fashion.
        section
          section#Functional
            h2 Functional Work
            ul
              li Dark Analysis
              li Geometric Distortion
              li Flat Fields
              li ACS Pipeline
          section
            h2 Dark Analysis
            p Look at how individual pixels evolve over time
            script(src='https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-latest.min.js')
            #StabilityPlot.plotly-graph-div(sytle='width: 100%; height: 100%;')
              script(src='../js/stabilityPlot.js', type='text/javascript')
          section
            h2 Geometric Distortion
            p With Vera Platais - ACS has pretty bad distortions...
            .row
              .col-sm-6
                img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/Before_distortion.png', alt='Before distortion correction')
              .col-sm-6
                img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/After_distortion.png', alt='After distortion correction')
          section
            h2 Flat Fields
            p Polarizers are complicated but cool
            div
              img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/polflat.png', alt='Polarizer Flats')
          section
            h2 ACS Reference File Pipeline
            p Maintain a piepline that REALLY needs to be rewritten
            iframe.giphy-embed(src='https://giphy.com/embed/fwxPSNMdhCEvu', width='480', height='270', frameborder='0', allowfullscreen='')
            p
              a(href='https://giphy.com/gifs/desk-fwxPSNMdhCEvu')
        section
          section#Science
            h2 Science Work
            ul
              li
                | New Horizons
                ul
                  li Pluto
                  li Kuiper Belt Objects
              li Cosmic Rays
              li Frontier Fields
          section
            h2 Pluto
            p Occultations of Pluto
            div
              img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/fig1_redo3_color.png', alt='Pluto Occultation')
          section
            h2 New Horizons
            p Searched for new KBOs for it to look at after Pluto encounter
            .row
              .col-sm-4
                img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/tripletDiscovery.png', alt='25.6 Mag object')
              .col-sm-4
                video(controls='')
                  source(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/VNH0001.mp4', type='video/mp4', alt='VNH0001')
                  |                                     I'm sorry; your browser doesn't support HTML5 video in WebM with VP8/VP9 or MP4 with H.264.
              .col-sm-4
                img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/HSTfield.png', alt='HST search field')
          section
            h2 Cosmic Rays
            p Science with calibration images!
            img(src='https://s3.amazonaws.com/vedadev/aboutmeSlides/dark.jpeg', alt='jcfubyecq')
          section
            h2 Frontier Fields
            p Frontier Fields pipeline team
            img(src='https://frontierfields.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/combo_abell_370.png', alt='Abell 370')
        section
          h2 Thats it for now
          iframe.giphy-embed(src='https://giphy.com/embed/NYrOxNlH7lwys', width='480', height='364', frameborder='0', allowfullscreen='')
          p
            a(href='https://giphy.com/gifs/end-NYrOxNlH7lwys')
